  "h1": "SEO Tools Guide: What to Use and When in 2027",
  "type": "tag",
  "title": "Insights on digital growth, AI search, and automation for SMEs.",
  "content_html": "",
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "What are the best free SEO tools?",
      "a": "<p>Google Search Console, Google Analytics 4, Google Business Profile, PageSpeed Insights and the Rich Results Test. Together they cover most needs of a small site.</p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "Do I need Ahrefs or Semrush?",
      "a": "<p>Not at the start. They help once you want to study rival links and keywords in depth, and one of the two is usually enough.</p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "Which tool shows my Google rankings?",
      "a": "<p>Google Search Console shows the searches your pages appear for, with clicks and average position. It is free.</p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I check my schema markup?",
      "a": "<p>Paste your page URL into Google's Rich Results Test. It lists each schema type it finds and flags any errors.</p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "Can tools do SEO for me?",
      "a": "<p>No. Tools find problems and show data, but people still fix pages and write content. Our <a href=\"/best-seo-services-in-india/\">SEO services</a> can do that work for you.</p>"
    }
  ],
